<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n605" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Actaeus</span></b> , a, um, adj., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀκταῖος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>pertaining to Attica</i>, <i>Attic</i>, <i>Athenian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in Actaeo Aracyntho,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 2, 24</span></i>
			 (as being on the border of Attica): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arces,</span>”
				<i>of Athens</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					2, 720</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fratres,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Clytos and Butes</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 7, 681</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mel Hymetti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					10, 386</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">imbres,</span>”
				<i>a rain of honey</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 4, 453</span></i>
			. —Hence, <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Actaei</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>the
				inhabitants of Attica</i>, <i><span class="en">Nep.
				Thras. 2, 1</span></i>.— <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Actaea</span></b> , ae, f., <i>a female Athenian; of Orithyia</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 6,
				711</span></i>.</div>
